---

This protocol outlines emergency management steps for cardiac arrest patients in the prehospital setting.

**Key Interventions:**
- Begin high-quality CPR immediately
- Apply defibrillator and analyze rhythm
- Administer Epinephrine 1mg IV/IO every 3-5 minutes
- Consider Amiodarone 300mg IV/IO after third shock

**Post-ROSC:**
- Maintain oxygen saturation 94-99%
- Monitor end-tidal CO2 (35-45 mmHg)
- Initiate transport to closest cardiac center

